Rombie's change to libretro-handy (Bro Code Technologies, 2026-10-29), for libretro-handy bc55d462. Handy's own files
are under its zlib license, whose second condition this header and the "Changed for Rombie" comments meet: "Altered
source versions must be plainly marked as such, and must not be misrepresented as being the original software."

The core is built without lynx/lynxdec.cpp, the decryption of a cart's loader that Handy's emulated boot ROM uses when
the player gives no lynxboot.img. The file states no license, so Rombie does not serve it. Changed:
- Makefile.common no longer compiles lynx/lynxdec.cpp; handy/build.sh also deletes it from the build's copy.
- CSystem::HLE_BIOS_FE4A, the emulated boot ROM's only call into it, no longer decrypts or loads anything.
- retro_load_game refuses a cart (returns false, with an error in the log) when there is no valid lynxboot.img,
  missing or failing Handy's CRC check, where Handy would otherwise fall back to the emulated boot ROM. A BS93
  homebrew file loads straight into RAM and still needs none.

